      "content": "Look for vague language regarding quality control or compliance; ambiguity often shelters poor performance or deliberate oversights. Specifically, check for insufficient indemnification clauses, as a weak clause means you bear more risk when things go wrong. Finally, examine their dispute resolution mechanism—a supplier strongly resistant to clear, structured mediation might be more inclined toward hidden tactics. These contractual indications can flag potential issues before they materialize.",
